{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"mcp_tool_call","server":"surface","tool":"save_skill","arguments":{"name":"json-xs-network-limits","content":"# json_xs formatting and web requests\nUse for tasks requesting JSON conversion or fetching live data with this program.\nThe run_program sandbox has no network access. json_xs can format supplied JSON but cannot download current exchange rates from the web in this environment. Do not invent rates or substitute stale data.\nRun args [\"-t\",\"json-pretty\"] with the exact supplied stdin to format JSON. Verified stdin '\\\"\\\"' yields stdout '\\\"\\\"\\n' with exit 0; this is an empty JSON string, not exchange-rate data.\n--help is unsupported (exit 255); usage is json_xs [-v] -f fromformat [-e code] [-t toformat].\nFor requests requiring live web downloads with empty input, report UNABLE and explain the network restriction. Check output contains the requested data, not merely valid JSON."},"result":null,"error":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
